      "writtenOn": "2019-08-22T19:32:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "CDP will be available on any port once current draw drops below 900mA on all active Type-A ports.  If a device was already plugged in on a second port and was not advertised CDP, it will not discover the newfound capability until re-plug (or connection reset, which is basically the same thing).\n\nI think this paragraph is correct only if we have 2 ports.  If we have 3 ports, then the following can (and will) happen:\n1. plug into port A, take 1.5A\n2. plug into port B, SDP limited to 0.9A\n3. unplug A. B stays at 0.9A (doesn\u0027t know about CDP)\n4. plug into port C without unplugging B, gets CDP/1.5A.",
